The loop that loads a process's regions into the PMP claims a bound of four,
and a process holds up to eight regions,
so the claim is false as soon as one holds five.
The code is the same, so only the counting harness catches it.

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -13,3 +13,3 @@
     for (unsigned i = 0; i < img->count; i++) {
-        LOOP_BOUND(PROCESS_REGION_SLOTS);
+        LOOP_BOUND(4);
         pmp_set(i, img->addr[i], img->cfg[i]);
